【Analysis】Two equal relationships are: the time required to travel downstream from $A$ to $C$ + the time required to drift downstream from $B$ to $C$ = the time required to travel downstream from $A$ to $B$ $\times \frac{43}{18} ;$ the time required to travel upstream from $B$ to $C$ + the repair time + the time required to travel upstream from $(A, C$ distance + 24 kilometers $)$ = the time required to travel upstream from $A$ to $B$. Substituting the relevant values will solve the problem.

【Solution】Let the distance between $A$ and $B$ be $x$ kilometers, and the distance between $A$ and $C$ be $y$ kilometers, then
$$
\begin{array}{l}
\text { we have }\left\{\begin{array}{l}
\frac{x}{40+24} \times \frac{43}{18}=\frac{y}{40+24}+\frac{x-y}{24} \\
\frac{x}{40-24}=\frac{x-y}{40-24}+1+\frac{y+24}{2 \times 40-24}
\end{array}\right. \\
\left\{\begin{array}{l}
\frac{x}{64} \times \frac{43}{18}=\frac{y}{64}+\frac{x-y}{24} \\
\frac{x}{16}=\frac{x-y}{16}+1+\frac{y+24}{56}
\end{array}\right. \\
\text { Solving, we get }\left\{\begin{array}{l}
x=192 \\
y=32
\end{array}\right.
\end{array}
$$

Answer: The distance between $A$ and $B$ is 192 kilometers.

